IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voc-common`

-- Victims of Crime Act 2001 (South Australia), Part 4 -- statutory compensation. SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE.
-- The rules are written in the Act's own actors and terms: "a person", "an immediate victim", "the claimant", "the
-- victim", "the offender", "the Crown Solicitor", "the Crown", "the court". The injured person's questions are in
-- voc-seat.l4, which IMPORTs this module and restates no rule.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 4(1) (child, dependants, immediate family, immediate victim, homicide, victim), s 4(2)
-- (indexation); s 17 (eligibility: injury, grief, dependants' financial loss, funeral expenses; the s 17(5) exclusions;
-- s 17(6) as a note); s 18 (the initial application period, the Crown Solicitor, the contents, the period for
-- negotiation, the court application and its last day, the court's extension as an input); s 19(2), (3) (service on the
-- offender); s 20(1), (3), (5), (5a), (7), (9) (the amounts, the caps, the bars as the court's findings, no interest);
-- s 21(1), (2) (medical examination); s 25(1) with the Victims of Crime (Statutory Compensation) Regulations 2019, reg 5
-- and Schedule 2 (legal costs); s 34 (assessment as at the offence); Schedule a1 (non-financial loss amounts); the
-- Regulations' reg 4 and Schedule 1 (what an application must contain).
--
-- Edition: the Victims of Crime Act 2001 as at 2021-01-01, deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/victims-of-crime-act-2001.txt, and the Victims of Crime (Statutory Compensation)
-- Regulations 2019 as at 2023-05-11, deposited at ../../../victims-of-crime-statutory-compensation-regulations-2019/
-- registers/source-bundle/victims-of-crime-statutory-compensation-regulations-2019.txt. Both are the Open Australian
-- Legal Corpus text (South Australian legislation last collected 2025-03-10), NOT the official text, and may be out of
-- date: the Act was listed at a version of 1.4.2025, so at least one later version is not reflected here. Based on
-- content from the South Australian Legislation website (CC BY 4.0).
--
-- NUMBERS THAT ARE INPUTS: the CPI (All groups index for Adelaide) figures that s 4(2) indexes by, and so every amount
-- marked "(indexed)" for an offence on or after 1 January 2016. No indexed figure is in any deposit.
-- NOT ENCODED: Parts 1 (other than s 4), 2, 3, 5, 6 and 7 (other than s 34); s 17(6) (recovery under the Return to
-- Work Act); s 18(4a), s 19(1), s 20(2), (4), (6), (8), (10), (11), ss 21(3)-(5), 22-24, 25(2), 26; Schedule 1
-- (repeal and transitional). The court's judgments in s 20(1), (4), (5), (5a), (7) and (8) are inputs.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage
-- table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Conventions. Money is in Australian dollars. Regulative clocks are in days.

§ `Victims of Crime Act 2001 (SA), Part 4 -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Coverage -- s 34, and the 2015 amendments`

-- s 34: "the amount of the compensation must be assessed in accordance with the provisions of this Act as in force at the
-- time of the commission of the offence". Sections 17, 20 and Schedule a1 took their present form from 1 July 2015 (the
-- Victims of Crime (Compensation) Amendment Act 2016, in operation from 1.7.2015, per the deposit's legislative history).
-- READING: an offence before 1 July 2015 is outside this encoding.
`the first day this encoding covers` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2015

GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is within this encoding` IF
    `the first day this encoding covers` `is on or before` `the day of the offence`

§§ `s 4(2) -- amounts marked (indexed)`

-- s 4(2): "if a monetary amount is followed by the word (indexed), the amount is (on or after 1 January 2016) to be
-- adjusted on 1 January of each year by multiplying the stated amount by a proportion obtained by dividing the CPI for the
-- September quarter of the immediately preceding year by the CPI for the September quarter, 2014, on the basis that the
-- quotient used for the purposes of the adjustment will be calculated to 2 decimal places and that the amount obtained
-- from the adjustment will be rounded to the nearest dollar." CPI: "the Consumer Price Index (All groups index for
-- Adelaide) published by the Australian Bureau of Statistics" (s 4(1)). The figures are not deposited: INPUTS.
-- The amount in force on a day is the one adjusted on the last 1 January on or before it (in that day's own year), using
-- the September quarter of the year before. Before 1 January 2016 the stated amount applies.
DECLARE `CPI figures for s 4(2)` HAS
    `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the adjustment` IS A NUMBER
    `CPI for the September quarter 2014`                               IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, cpi IS A `CPI figures for s 4(2)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 4(2) proportion in force on` `the day` `with` cpi MEANS
    IF DATE_YEAR `the day` LESS THAN 2016
    THEN 1
    ELSE `rounded to 2 decimal places` (cpi's `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the adjustment` DIVIDED BY cpi's `CPI for the September quarter 2014`)

GIVEN `the stated amount` IS A NUMBER, `the proportion` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the indexed amount of` `the stated amount` `at` `the proportion` MEANS
    `rounded to the nearest dollar` (`the stated amount` TIMES `the proportion`)

-- The stated amounts of s 20 and Schedule a1.
`the overall limit, before indexation (s 20(3))`      MEANS 100000
`the grief limit, before indexation (s 20(1)(c))`     MEANS 20000
`the funeral limit, before indexation (s 20(1)(d))`   MEANS 14000
-- s 20(3)(a)(i): "$2 000" is NOT followed by "(indexed)", so it stays $2 000.
`the financial loss threshold (s 20(3)(a)(i))`        MEANS 2000

DECLARE `Indexed amounts` HAS
    `the s 4(2) proportion`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `the overall limit (s 20(3)(a)(iii), (c))`                    IS A NUMBER
    `the most for grief (s 20(1)(c))`                             IS A NUMBER
    `the most for funeral expenses (s 20(1)(d))`                  IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE, cpi IS A `CPI figures for s 4(2)`
GIVETH AN `Indexed amounts`
`the indexed amounts for an offence on` `the day of the offence` `with` cpi MEANS
    `Indexed amounts` WITH
        `the s 4(2) proportion`                       IS p
        `the overall limit (s 20(3)(a)(iii), (c))`    IS `the indexed amount of` `the overall limit, before indexation (s 20(3))` `at` p
        `the most for grief (s 20(1)(c))`             IS `the indexed amount of` `the grief limit, before indexation (s 20(1)(c))` `at` p
        `the most for funeral expenses (s 20(1)(d))`  IS `the indexed amount of` `the funeral limit, before indexation (s 20(1)(d))` `at` p
    WHERE
        p MEANS `the s 4(2) proportion in force on` `the day of the offence` `with` cpi

§§ `s 4(1) -- immediate family, immediate victim`

-- s 4(1) "immediate family of a person means any one or more of the following: (a) a spouse or domestic partner; (b) a
-- parent; (c) a grandparent; (d) a child (including an adult child); (e) a grandchild (including an adult grandchild);
-- (f) a brother or sister". "parent includes a person who stands in the position, and undertakes the responsibilities,
-- of a parent"; a child likewise. "spouse": legally married; "domestic partner": within the Family Relationships Act 1975
-- (a borrowed term, asked as a fact).
DECLARE `Family relationship` IS ONE OF
    `a spouse or domestic partner`
    `a parent`
    `a grandparent`
    `a child, including an adult child`
    `a grandchild, including an adult grandchild`
    `a brother or sister`
    `none of these`

GIVEN r IS A `Family relationship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a member of the immediate family` r IF NOT (r EQUALS `none of these`)

-- s 4(1) "victim, in relation to an offence, means a person who suffers harm as a result of the commission of the offence
-- (but does not include a person who was a party to the commission of the offence)"; "harm means injury, damage or loss";
-- "injury means physical or mental injury, and includes pregnancy, mental shock and nervous shock".
-- "immediate victim ... means a victim of any of the following classes: (a) a person who suffers physical injury as a
-- result of the commission of the offence; (b) a person who suffers psychological injury as a result of being directly
-- involved in the circumstances of the offence or in operations in the immediate aftermath of the offence to deal with its
-- consequences; (c) if the offence was committed against a child -- a parent or guardian of the child; (d) if the offence
-- was committed against a person who dies as a result of the offence -- a member of the immediate family of the deceased".
-- "offence includes conduct ... that would constitute an offence if it were not for that person's age or mental
-- impairment" (so an offender too young or impaired to be convicted still commits an "offence" here).
DECLARE `The person and the offence` HAS
    `the person suffered physical injury as a result of the offence`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person suffered psychological injury from being directly involved in the offence or its immediate aftermath` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person suffered other harm (injury, damage or loss) as a result of the offence`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence was committed against a child of whom the person is a parent or guardian`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person's relationship to someone who died as a result of the offence`                              IS A `Family relationship`
    `the person was a party to the commission of the offence`                                              IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN p IS A `The person and the offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a victim of the offence` p IF
        (NOT p's `the person was a party to the commission of the offence`)
    AND (   p's `the person suffered physical injury as a result of the offence`
         OR p's `the person suffered psychological injury from being directly involved in the offence or its immediate aftermath`
         OR p's `the person suffered other harm (injury, damage or loss) as a result of the offence`)

GIVEN p IS A `The person and the offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an immediate victim of the offence` p IF
        `is a victim of the offence` p
    AND (   p's `the person suffered physical injury as a result of the offence`
         OR p's `the person suffered psychological injury from being directly involved in the offence or its immediate aftermath`
         OR p's `the offence was committed against a child of whom the person is a parent or guardian`
         OR `is a member of the immediate family` (p's `the person's relationship to someone who died as a result of the offence`))

§§ `s 17 -- eligibility to claim`

-- s 17(1)(b): "at least one of the following conditions is satisfied: (i) the offence involved the use of violence or a
-- threat of violence against the person or a member of the person's immediate family; (ii) the offence created a
-- reasonable apprehension of imminent harm to the person or a member of the person's immediate family; (iii) the offence
-- is a sexual offence; (iv) the offence caused death or physical injury."
-- s 4(1) "homicide means murder, manslaughter or an offence against section 14 of the Criminal Law Consolidation Act 1935
-- (criminal neglect) where the victim dies" (asked as a fact).
DECLARE `The offence` HAS
    `the day the offence was committed`                                                                     IS A DATE
    `it involved violence or a threat of violence against the person or a member of the person's immediate family` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it created a reasonable apprehension of imminent harm to the person or a member of the person's immediate family` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a sexual offence`                                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `it caused death or physical injury`                                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a homicide`                                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 17(5): "However -- (a) a person is not entitled to statutory compensation if the injury arises from a breach of
-- statutory duty by the person's employer that occurs in the course of the person's employment; and (b) ... if the person
-- has received, or is entitled to receive, a payment or damages in respect of death or non-economic loss for the same harm
-- under the Return to Work Act 2014; and (c) ... if the injury is caused by, or arises out of the use of, a motor vehicle
-- in circumstances in which the injury falls within the ambit of a compulsory third-party insurance scheme covering the
-- motor vehicle (whether the vehicle is in fact insured under the scheme or an action for damages lies against a nominal
-- defendant); and (d) ... for hospital or medical expenses that would, if no award for compensation were made, be
-- recoverable from a health fund or scheme; and (e) a prisoner is not entitled to statutory compensation for psychological
-- injury resulting from an offence committed in the prison unless the prisoner was assaulted or suffered physical injury."
-- Whether an injury "falls within the ambit" of a CTP scheme is a borrowed term here; ctp-core.l4 works it out from the
-- Motor Vehicles Act 1959, and the seat joins the two. (d) removes those expenses from the financial loss only: the
-- financial loss is asked net of them. READING: (a) and (e) speak of the person's own injury and employment, so they are
-- applied to a claim for the person's own injury only; (b) and (c) are applied to every claim arising from the injury,
-- including grief, the dependants' loss and funeral expenses.
DECLARE `Section 17(5) facts` HAS
    `the injury arises from a breach of statutory duty by the person's employer in the course of the person's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has received or is entitled to a Return to Work payment or damages for death or non-economic loss for the same harm` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury falls within the ambit of a compulsory third-party insurance scheme covering a motor vehicle`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a prisoner claiming for psychological injury from an offence committed in the prison`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the prisoner was assaulted or suffered physical injury`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Eligibility` IS ONE OF
    `eligible to claim`
    `not eligible: not an immediate victim of the offence (s 4(1), s 17(1)(a))`
    `not eligible: the offence meets none of the conditions in s 17(1)(b)`
    `not eligible for grief: the death was not caused by a homicide (s 17(2))`
    `not eligible for grief: not the spouse or domestic partner, a child under 18, or the parent of a child victim (s 17(2))`
    `not eligible for the dependants' financial loss: the conditions of s 17(3) are not met`
    `not eligible for funeral expenses: the conditions of s 17(4) are not met`
    `not entitled: the injury arises from the employer's breach of statutory duty (s 17(5)(a))`
    `not entitled: a Return to Work payment or damages covers the same harm (s 17(5)(b))`
    `not entitled: the injury falls within a compulsory third-party insurance scheme (s 17(5)(c))`
    `not entitled: a prisoner's psychological injury from an offence in the prison (s 17(5)(e))`
    `not covered: an offence before 1 July 2015`

GIVEN x IS A `Section 17(5) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Eligibility`
`the s 17(5)(b), (c) exclusion` x MEANS
    IF x's `the person has received or is entitled to a Return to Work payment or damages for death or non-economic loss for the same harm`
    THEN JUST `not entitled: a Return to Work payment or damages covers the same harm (s 17(5)(b))`
    ELSE IF x's `the injury falls within the ambit of a compulsory third-party insurance scheme covering a motor vehicle`
         THEN JUST `not entitled: the injury falls within a compulsory third-party insurance scheme (s 17(5)(c))`
         ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN x IS A `Section 17(5) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Eligibility`
`the s 17(5) exclusion for the person's own injury` x MEANS
    IF x's `the injury arises from a breach of statutory duty by the person's employer in the course of the person's employment`
    THEN JUST `not entitled: the injury arises from the employer's breach of statutory duty (s 17(5)(a))`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the s 17(5)(b), (c) exclusion` x
         WHEN JUST e THEN JUST e
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             IF     x's `the person is a prisoner claiming for psychological injury from an offence committed in the prison`
                AND (NOT x's `the prisoner was assaulted or suffered physical injury`)
             THEN JUST `not entitled: a prisoner's psychological injury from an offence in the prison (s 17(5)(e))`
             ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the exclusion` IS A MAYBE `Eligibility`
GIVETH AN `Eligibility`
`eligible unless` `the exclusion` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the exclusion`
    WHEN JUST e THEN e
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `eligible to claim`

-- s 17(1): "A person is eligible to claim statutory compensation for injury caused by an offence if -- (a) the person is
-- an immediate victim of the offence; and (b) at least one of the following conditions is satisfied".
GIVEN o IS A `The offence`, p IS A `The person and the offence`, x IS A `Section 17(5) facts`
GIVETH AN `Eligibility`
`s 17(1) -- eligibility to claim for injury` o p x MEANS
    IF NOT (`the offence is within this encoding` (o's `the day the offence was committed`))
    THEN `not covered: an offence before 1 July 2015`
    ELSE IF NOT (`is an immediate victim of the offence` p)
         THEN `not eligible: not an immediate victim of the offence (s 4(1), s 17(1)(a))`
         ELSE IF NOT (   o's `it involved violence or a threat of violence against the person or a member of the person's immediate family`
                      OR o's `it created a reasonable apprehension of imminent harm to the person or a member of the person's immediate family`
                      OR o's `it is a sexual offence`
                      OR o's `it caused death or physical injury`)
              THEN `not eligible: the offence meets none of the conditions in s 17(1)(b)`
              ELSE `eligible unless` (`the s 17(5) exclusion for the person's own injury` x)

-- s 17(2): "A person is eligible to claim statutory compensation for grief suffered in consequence of the commission of a
-- homicide if the person is -- (a) a spouse or domestic partner of the deceased victim; or (ab) a child of the deceased
-- victim (if the child was under the age of 18 at the time of the offence); or (b) where the deceased victim was a child --
-- a parent of the deceased victim." "child" does not, "in the absence of an indication to the contrary, extend to an
-- adult child" (s 4(1)): READING, "the deceased victim was a child" means under 18 when the victim died.
DECLARE `Relationship to the deceased` IS ONE OF
    `the spouse or domestic partner of the deceased`
    `a child of the deceased, under 18 at the time of the offence`
    `a child of the deceased, 18 or over at the time of the offence`
    `a parent of the deceased`
    `some other relationship, or none`

GIVEN o IS A `The offence`
      r IS A `Relationship to the deceased`
      `the deceased was under 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      x IS A `Section 17(5) facts`
GIVETH AN `Eligibility`
`s 17(2) -- eligibility to claim for grief` o r `the deceased was under 18` x MEANS
    IF NOT (`the offence is within this encoding` (o's `the day the offence was committed`))
    THEN `not covered: an offence before 1 July 2015`
    ELSE IF NOT (o's `it is a homicide`)
         THEN `not eligible for grief: the death was not caused by a homicide (s 17(2))`
         ELSE IF     (NOT (r EQUALS `the spouse or domestic partner of the deceased`))
                 AND (NOT (r EQUALS `a child of the deceased, under 18 at the time of the offence`))
                 AND (NOT (r EQUALS `a parent of the deceased` AND `the deceased was under 18`))
              THEN `not eligible for grief: not the spouse or domestic partner, a child under 18, or the parent of a child victim (s 17(2))`
              ELSE `eligible unless` (`the s 17(5)(b), (c) exclusion` x)

-- s 17(3): "A person is eligible to claim statutory compensation for financial loss suffered by the dependants of a
-- deceased victim if -- (a) the victim died as a result of the injury caused by the offence; and (b) no previous order for
-- statutory compensation has been made in respect of the injury; and (c) the person is, in the opinion of the court, a
-- suitable person to represent the interests of the dependants." (c) is the court's opinion: an INPUT.
-- s 4(1) "dependants ... means any spouse, domestic partner, parents or children (including adult children) of the victim
-- who are financially dependent on the victim".
GIVEN o IS A `The offence`
      `the victim died as a result of the injury caused by the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a previous order for statutory compensation has been made in respect of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers the person suitable to represent the dependants` IS A BOOLEAN
      x IS A `Section 17(5) facts`
GIVETH AN `Eligibility`
`s 17(3) -- eligibility to claim for the dependants' financial loss` o `the victim died as a result of the injury caused by the offence` `a previous order for statutory compensation has been made in respect of the injury` `the court considers the person suitable to represent the dependants` x MEANS
    IF NOT (`the offence is within this encoding` (o's `the day the offence was committed`))
    THEN `not covered: an offence before 1 July 2015`
    ELSE IF     `the victim died as a result of the injury caused by the offence`
            AND (NOT `a previous order for statutory compensation has been made in respect of the injury`)
            AND `the court considers the person suitable to represent the dependants`
         THEN `eligible unless` (`the s 17(5)(b), (c) exclusion` x)
         ELSE `not eligible for the dependants' financial loss: the conditions of s 17(3) are not met`

-- s 17(4): "A person is eligible to claim statutory compensation for funeral expenses if -- (a) a victim dies in
-- consequence of the offence; and (b) the person has paid, or is responsible for payment of, the victim's funeral
-- expenses."
GIVEN o IS A `The offence`
      `a victim died in consequence of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has paid or is responsible for paying the funeral expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
      x IS A `Section 17(5) facts`
GIVETH AN `Eligibility`
`s 17(4) -- eligibility to claim funeral expenses` o `a victim died in consequence of the offence` `the person has paid or is responsible for paying the funeral expenses` x MEANS
    IF NOT (`the offence is within this encoding` (o's `the day the offence was committed`))
    THEN `not covered: an offence before 1 July 2015`
    ELSE IF `a victim died in consequence of the offence` AND `the person has paid or is responsible for paying the funeral expenses`
         THEN `eligible unless` (`the s 17(5)(b), (c) exclusion` x)
         ELSE `not eligible for funeral expenses: the conditions of s 17(4) are not met`

§§ `s 18 -- the application, the period for negotiation and the court`

-- s 18(2): "The initial application period is -- (a) for an application by a victim -- 3 years after the commission of the
-- offence; (b) for an application arising from the death of a victim -- 12 months after the date of death."
-- READING: an application for the person's own injury is "an application by a victim"; one for grief, the dependants'
-- loss or funeral expenses "arises from the death". The Act does not say which applies to a family member's own
-- psychological injury after a homicide (both could); this encoding treats it as an application by a victim.
DECLARE `Kind of application` IS ONE OF
    `an application by a victim for the victim's own injury`
    `an application arising from the death of a victim`

`the months in the initial application period of a victim (s 18(2)(a))`         MEANS 36
`the months in the initial application period after a death (s 18(2)(b))`       MEANS 12

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of application`, `the day of the offence` IS A DATE, `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the initial application period` k `the day of the offence` `the day of death` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an application by a victim for the victim's own injury`
        THEN `the day of the offence` `plus months` `the months in the initial application period of a victim (s 18(2)(a))`
    WHEN `an application arising from the death of a victim`
        THEN `the day of death` `plus months` `the months in the initial application period after a death (s 18(2)(b))`

-- s 18(7): "The court may, for any proper reason, extend a period of limitation fixed by this section." The court's
-- extension is an INPUT; an extension can only lengthen the period.
GIVEN `the last day` IS A DATE, `the court has extended the period` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day it was extended to` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day, as extended under s 18(7)` `the last day` `the court has extended the period` `the day it was extended to` MEANS
    IF `the court has extended the period`
    THEN `the later of the days` `the last day` `and` `the day it was extended to`
    ELSE `the last day`

-- s 18(5): "If a claim for statutory compensation has not been settled by agreement between the Crown Solicitor and the
-- claimant within 3 months after the application is made or a longer period agreed between the Crown Solicitor and the
-- claimant (the period for negotiation), the claimant may apply to the court". A shorter period is not "a longer period",
-- so 3 months is the least.
`the months in the period for negotiation (s 18(5))` MEANS 3

GIVEN `the day of the application` IS A DATE, `a longer period was agreed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day the agreed period ends` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the period for negotiation` `the day of the application` `a longer period was agreed` `the day the agreed period ends` MEANS
    IF `a longer period was agreed`
    THEN `the later of the days` `the three months` `and` `the day the agreed period ends`
    ELSE `the three months`
    WHERE
        `the three months` MEANS `the day of the application` `plus months` `the months in the period for negotiation (s 18(5))`

-- s 18(6): "An application to the court under subsection (5) must be made on or before the later of the following: (a) the
-- end of the initial application period; or (b) the end of the period of 6 months that follows immediately after the end
-- of the period for negotiation."
`the months after the period for negotiation (s 18(6)(b))` MEANS 6

GIVEN `the end of the initial application period` IS A DATE, `the end of the period for negotiation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply to the court (s 18(6))` `the end of the initial application period` `the end of the period for negotiation` MEANS
    `the later of the days` `the end of the initial application period` `and` (`the end of the period for negotiation` `plus months` `the months after the period for negotiation (s 18(6)(b))`)

-- s 18(4), reg 4 and Schedule 1 of the Regulations: what an application must contain or be accompanied by. Clause numbers
-- are the Regulations' Schedule 1 (clauses 3 and 9 were deleted in 2023). "limited claim" (reg 3): a claim limited to
-- grief, funeral expenses, or both.
DECLARE `Application item` IS ONE OF
    `the claimant's name, address and date of birth (Sch 1 cl 1(a))`
    `the victim's name, address and date of birth (cl 1(b))`
    `the date, time and place of the offence, its nature and the details of what happened (cl 1(c), (d))`
    `when and where the offence was reported to police, or why it was not (cl 1(e))`
    `the nature and extent of the injury (cl 1(f))`
    `the nature of the claimant's relationship to the victim (cl 1(g))`
    `the claimant's relationship to the victim, the date of death and the date of the funeral (cl 1(h))`
    `the offender's name and address if known, the outcome of any prosecution, and whether the claimant gave evidence for the prosecution and if not why (cl 2)`
    `an itemised list of funeral expenses (cl 4(1))`
    `particulars of the special damages and loss of earnings claimed (cl 4(2))`
    `a formulated claim: the points claimed for non-financial loss, the amounts claimed for past loss of earnings, loss of earning capacity and special damages, and all amounts received or likely from other sources (cl 5)`
    `copies of 2 identification documents, at least 1 with a photograph, certified by a legal practitioner, justice or police officer (cl 6)`
    `copies of documents confirming the relationship to the victim (cl 7)`
    `a hospital report (up to 20 pages) or a report from a general medical practitioner or dentist (cl 8)`
    `a letter from the employer or the employer's insurer, or other written evidence, of the period and amount of earnings lost (cl 10(1)(a))`
    `written evidence of the period and amount of earnings lost as a self-employed person (cl 10(1)(b))`
    `a letter from the person offering the work, or other written evidence, of the work and its value (cl 10(2))`
    `income tax returns for the 5 financial years before the offence, the year of the offence and each year since (cl 10(3))`
    `copies of documents about amounts received or likely to be received from the offender, an insurer or any other source (cl 11)`
    `any medical reports relevant to the injury that the claimant has or can get (s 18(4)(a)(ii))`
    `verification of the information by statutory declaration (s 18(4)(b))`

DECLARE `What the application claims` HAS
    `the claimant is not the victim`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant relies on a relationship to the victim`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim is dead`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim is limited to grief, funeral expenses or both`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim is limited to funeral expenses`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `special damages or loss of earnings are claimed`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `past loss of earnings is claimed as an employee`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `past loss of earnings is claimed as a self-employed person`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `loss of earnings from a contract the injury prevented is claimed`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `loss of earning capacity is claimed`                                  IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN item IS AN `Application item`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Application item`
`always` item MEANS LIST item

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN, item IS AN `Application item`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Application item`
`only if` b item MEANS IF b THEN LIST item ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN a IS A `What the application claims`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Application item`
`what the application must contain (s 18(4), reg 4, Schedule 1)` a MEANS
    concat (LIST
        `always` `the claimant's name, address and date of birth (Sch 1 cl 1(a))`,
        `only if` (a's `the claimant is not the victim`) `the victim's name, address and date of birth (cl 1(b))`,
        `always` `the date, time and place of the offence, its nature and the details of what happened (cl 1(c), (d))`,
        `always` `when and where the offence was reported to police, or why it was not (cl 1(e))`,
        `always` `the nature and extent of the injury (cl 1(f))`,
        `only if` (a's `the claimant relies on a relationship to the victim`) `the nature of the claimant's relationship to the victim (cl 1(g))`,
        `only if` (a's `the victim is dead`) `the claimant's relationship to the victim, the date of death and the date of the funeral (cl 1(h))`,
        `always` `the offender's name and address if known, the outcome of any prosecution, and whether the claimant gave evidence for the prosecution and if not why (cl 2)`,
        `only if` (a's `the claim is limited to funeral expenses`) `an itemised list of funeral expenses (cl 4(1))`,
        `only if` (a's `special damages or loss of earnings are claimed`) `particulars of the special damages and loss of earnings claimed (cl 4(2))`,
        `only if` (NOT a's `the claim is limited to grief, funeral expenses or both`) `a formulated claim: the points claimed for non-financial loss, the amounts claimed for past loss of earnings, loss of earning capacity and special damages, and all amounts received or likely from other sources (cl 5)`,
        `always` `copies of 2 identification documents, at least 1 with a photograph, certified by a legal practitioner, justice or police officer (cl 6)`,
        `only if` (a's `the claimant relies on a relationship to the victim`) `copies of documents confirming the relationship to the victim (cl 7)`,
        `only if` (NOT a's `the claim is limited to grief, funeral expenses or both`) `a hospital report (up to 20 pages) or a report from a general medical practitioner or dentist (cl 8)`,
        `only if` (a's `past loss of earnings is claimed as an employee`) `a letter from the employer or the employer's insurer, or other written evidence, of the period and amount of earnings lost (cl 10(1)(a))`,
        `only if` (a's `past loss of earnings is claimed as a self-employed person`) `written evidence of the period and amount of earnings lost as a self-employed person (cl 10(1)(b))`,
        `only if` (a's `loss of earnings from a contract the injury prevented is claimed`) `a letter from the person offering the work, or other written evidence, of the work and its value (cl 10(2))`,
        `only if` (a's `loss of earning capacity is claimed`) `income tax returns for the 5 financial years before the offence, the year of the offence and each year since (cl 10(3))`,
        `always` `copies of documents about amounts received or likely to be received from the offender, an insurer or any other source (cl 11)`,
        `always` `any medical reports relevant to the injury that the claimant has or can get (s 18(4)(a)(ii))`,
        `always` `verification of the information by statutory declaration (s 18(4)(b))`)

§§ `s 20 -- the amounts`

-- Schedule a1, "Compensation amounts for non-financial loss (section 20(3)(a))": the corresponding amount for each
-- numerical value 1 to 60, each "(indexed)", in the deposit's order. Values 1 and 2 have amounts in the Schedule, but
-- s 20(3)(a)(ii) says that at 2 or less "no award will be made for non-financial loss" (finding 4).
`the Schedule a1 amounts, before indexation` MEANS
    LIST 1000, 2000, 4000, 5000, 6000, 7000, 8000, 9000, 10000, 11000,
         12000, 13000, 14000, 15000, 16000, 17000, 18000, 19000, 20000, 21000,
         22000, 23000, 24000, 25000, 26000, 27000, 28000, 29000, 30000, 31000,
         32867, 34733, 36600, 38467, 40333, 42200, 44067, 45933, 47800, 49667,
         52000, 54333, 56667, 59000, 61333, 63667, 66000, 68333, 70667, 73000,
         75800, 78600, 81400, 84200, 87000, 89800, 92600, 95400, 98200, 100000

GIVEN v IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a value on the s 20(3)(a)(ii) scale` v IF
    `is a whole number` v AND v AT LEAST 0 AND v AT MOST 60

-- s 20(3)(a)(ii): "the total non-financial loss must be assigned a numerical value on a scale running from 0 to 60 ...;
-- and if the numerical value so assigned is 2 or less, no award will be made for non-financial loss but, if the numerical
-- value exceeds 2, the amount awarded will be the amount determined in accordance with Schedule a1 as corresponding to the
-- number so assigned". The value is the court's: an INPUT. READING: Schedule a1 has whole numbers only.
GIVEN v IS A NUMBER, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 20(3)(a)(ii) amount for non-financial loss at scale value` v `at` p MEANS
    IF v AT MOST 2
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the indexed amount of` (at `the Schedule a1 amounts, before indexation` (v MINUS 1)) `at` p

-- s 20(3)(a)(i): "if financial loss is to be compensated and the amount that would, but for this subparagraph, be awarded
-- exceeds $2 000, the amount awarded will, subject to subparagraph (iii), be $2 000 plus three-quarters of the excess".
-- The amount the court would otherwise award is an INPUT (with s 17(5)(d) expenses left out).
GIVEN `the financial loss` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 20(3)(a)(i) amount for financial loss of` `the financial loss` MEANS
    IF `the financial loss` GREATER THAN `the financial loss threshold (s 20(3)(a)(i))`
    THEN `the financial loss threshold (s 20(3)(a)(i))` PLUS (0.75 TIMES (`the financial loss` MINUS `the financial loss threshold (s 20(3)(a)(i))`))
    ELSE `the financial loss`

-- The court's findings that bar an order (inputs). s 20(5): no order for injury to a claimant if the court "(a) is
-- satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that the injury to the claimant occurred while the claimant was engaged in conduct
-- constituting an indictable offence; and (b) is satisfied on the balance of probabilities that the claimant's conduct
-- contributed materially to the risk of injury" (s 20(5a): to the death, for grief or funeral expenses), "unless the court
-- is satisfied that ... failure to compensate would be unjust". s 20(7): no order "if it appears to the court that the
-- claimant, without good reason -- (a) failed to report the offence to the police within a reasonable time ...; or (b)
-- refused or failed to provide information to the police ... as to the offender's identity or whereabouts; or (c) refused
-- or failed to give evidence in the prosecution ...; or (d) otherwise refused or failed to co-operate properly ... and, in
-- consequence, investigation or prosecution of the offence was not commenced or was terminated or hindered to a
-- significant extent." s 20(4) (the victim's contributing conduct) and (8) (failure to mitigate) go to the amount: the
-- financial loss and scale value inputs are the court's, after them.
DECLARE `Court findings under s 20` HAS
    `the court finds the claimant's indictable conduct contributed materially to the injury or death (s 20(5), (5a))` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court finds that failure to compensate would be unjust`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court finds a failure without good reason to report or co-operate that hindered the case (s 20(7))`        IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN f IS A `Court findings under s 20`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20(5) or (5a) bars the order` f IF
        f's `the court finds the claimant's indictable conduct contributed materially to the injury or death (s 20(5), (5a))`
    AND (NOT f's `the court finds that failure to compensate would be unjust`)

DECLARE `Award` IS ONE OF
    `the award is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no order: the claimant's indictable conduct contributed materially (s 20(5) or (5a))`
    `no order: the claimant failed without good reason to report or co-operate (s 20(7))`
    `not covered: an offence before 1 July 2015`
    `not covered: the scale value must be a whole number from 0 to 60 (s 20(3)(a)(ii), Schedule a1)`

-- s 20(1)(a) and (3)(a), (iii): "where an amount arrived at to compensate financial loss, or the aggregate of amounts
-- arrived at to compensate financial loss and non-financial loss, would, but for this subparagraph, exceed $100 000
-- (indexed), the amount awarded will be $100 000 (indexed)". s 20(9): "No interest may be awarded".
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE
      cpi IS A `CPI figures for s 4(2)`
      `the financial loss` IS A NUMBER
      `the scale value` IS A NUMBER
      f IS A `Court findings under s 20`
GIVETH AN `Award`
`s 20(1)(a), (3)(a) -- the award for injury` `the day of the offence` cpi `the financial loss` `the scale value` f MEANS
    IF NOT (`the offence is within this encoding` `the day of the offence`)
    THEN `not covered: an offence before 1 July 2015`
    ELSE IF NOT (`is a value on the s 20(3)(a)(ii) scale` `the scale value`)
         THEN `not covered: the scale value must be a whole number from 0 to 60 (s 20(3)(a)(ii), Schedule a1)`
         ELSE IF `s 20(5) or (5a) bars the order` f
              THEN `no order: the claimant's indictable conduct contributed materially (s 20(5) or (5a))`
              ELSE IF f's `the court finds a failure without good reason to report or co-operate that hindered the case (s 20(7))`
                   THEN `no order: the claimant failed without good reason to report or co-operate (s 20(7))`
                   ELSE `the award is` (`the smaller number of` (`the s 20(3)(a)(i) amount for financial loss of` `the financial loss` PLUS `the s 20(3)(a)(ii) amount for non-financial loss at scale value` `the scale value` `at` (amounts's `the s 4(2) proportion`)) `and` (amounts's `the overall limit (s 20(3)(a)(iii), (c))`))
    WHERE
        amounts MEANS `the indexed amounts for an offence on` `the day of the offence` `with` cpi

-- s 20(1)(b): "that the dependants of a dead victim be paid ... such amount as the court thinks fit by way of compensation
-- for the financial loss suffered by them (to be proportioned between the various claimants as the court thinks fit)";
-- s 20(3)(a) applies to an award under (1)(b) too: the $2 000 rule and the cap. READING: s 20(5) speaks of "injury to a
-- claimant" and (5a) of grief and funeral expenses, so only s 20(7) can bar this order.
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE
      cpi IS A `CPI figures for s 4(2)`
      `the dependants' financial loss` IS A NUMBER
      f IS A `Court findings under s 20`
GIVETH AN `Award`
`s 20(1)(b), (3)(a) -- the award for the dependants' financial loss` `the day of the offence` cpi `the dependants' financial loss` f MEANS
    IF NOT (`the offence is within this encoding` `the day of the offence`)
    THEN `not covered: an offence before 1 July 2015`
    ELSE IF f's `the court finds a failure without good reason to report or co-operate that hindered the case (s 20(7))`
         THEN `no order: the claimant failed without good reason to report or co-operate (s 20(7))`
         ELSE `the award is` (`the smaller number of` (`the s 20(3)(a)(i) amount for financial loss of` `the dependants' financial loss`) `and` (amounts's `the overall limit (s 20(3)(a)(iii), (c))`))
    WHERE
        amounts MEANS `the indexed amounts for an offence on` `the day of the offence` `with` cpi

-- s 20(1)(c): "in the case of an application for compensation for grief -- that a claimant be paid by the Crown such
-- amount (not exceeding $20 000 (indexed)) as the Court thinks fit". The amount the court thinks fit is an INPUT.
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE
      cpi IS A `CPI figures for s 4(2)`
      `the amount the court thinks fit for grief` IS A NUMBER
      f IS A `Court findings under s 20`
GIVETH AN `Award`
`s 20(1)(c) -- the award for grief` `the day of the offence` cpi `the amount the court thinks fit for grief` f MEANS
    IF NOT (`the offence is within this encoding` `the day of the offence`)
    THEN `not covered: an offence before 1 July 2015`
    ELSE IF `s 20(5) or (5a) bars the order` f
         THEN `no order: the claimant's indictable conduct contributed materially (s 20(5) or (5a))`
         ELSE IF f's `the court finds a failure without good reason to report or co-operate that hindered the case (s 20(7))`
              THEN `no order: the claimant failed without good reason to report or co-operate (s 20(7))`
              ELSE `the award is` (`the smaller number of` `the amount the court thinks fit for grief` `and` (amounts's `the most for grief (s 20(1)(c))`))
    WHERE
        amounts MEANS `the indexed amounts for an offence on` `the day of the offence` `with` cpi

-- s 20(1)(d): "in the case of an application for compensation for funeral expenses -- that the claimant be paid -- (i) the
-- amount of funeral expenses incurred by the claimant; or (ii) $14 000 (indexed), whichever is the lesser."
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE
      cpi IS A `CPI figures for s 4(2)`
      `the funeral expenses incurred` IS A NUMBER
      f IS A `Court findings under s 20`
GIVETH AN `Award`
`s 20(1)(d) -- the award for funeral expenses` `the day of the offence` cpi `the funeral expenses incurred` f MEANS
    IF NOT (`the offence is within this encoding` `the day of the offence`)
    THEN `not covered: an offence before 1 July 2015`
    ELSE IF `s 20(5) or (5a) bars the order` f
         THEN `no order: the claimant's indictable conduct contributed materially (s 20(5) or (5a))`
         ELSE IF f's `the court finds a failure without good reason to report or co-operate that hindered the case (s 20(7))`
              THEN `no order: the claimant failed without good reason to report or co-operate (s 20(7))`
              ELSE `the award is` (`the smaller number of` `the funeral expenses incurred` `and` (amounts's `the most for funeral expenses (s 20(1)(d))`))
    WHERE
        amounts MEANS `the indexed amounts for an offence on` `the day of the offence` `with` cpi

-- s 20(3)(c): "statutory compensation amounting in aggregate to more than $100 000 (indexed) cannot be awarded to any
-- single claimant", subject to: "1 If the claimant claims both as a dependant or representative of the dependants of a
-- deceased victim and in some other capacity, the limitation applies separately to each capacity in which the claimant
-- claims. 2 An amount to which an applicant is entitled by way of funeral expenses will not be brought into account".
GIVEN `the award for injury` IS A NUMBER
      `the award for grief` IS A NUMBER
      `the award for the dependants' financial loss` IS A NUMBER
      `the award for funeral expenses` IS A NUMBER
      `the overall limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 20(3)(c) -- the most one claimant can be awarded in all` `the award for injury` `the award for grief` `the award for the dependants' financial loss` `the award for funeral expenses` `the overall limit` MEANS
        `the smaller number of` (`the award for injury` PLUS `the award for grief`) `and` `the overall limit`
    PLUS `the smaller number of` `the award for the dependants' financial loss` `and` `the overall limit`
    PLUS `the award for funeral expenses`

-- s 20(9): "No interest may be awarded by the court in respect of the whole or any part of the amount of statutory
-- compensation ordered."
`interest may be awarded on statutory compensation (s 20(9))` MEANS FALSE

§§ `s 25(1), Regulations reg 5 and Schedule 2 -- legal costs`

-- s 25(1): "(a) costs awarded in proceedings under this Act must not exceed the amounts prescribed by regulation in
-- relation to such costs (plus GST) as at the time of commencement of the proceedings; and (b) a legal practitioner must
-- neither charge nor seek to recover ... an amount by way of costs in excess of the amount prescribed by regulation ...
-- (plus GST) as at the time of commencement of the proceedings." The amounts are in Schedule 2, each "(indexed)". The
-- Regulations do not say how "(indexed)" works; READING: as s 4(2) of the Act says, at the time the proceedings commence
-- (finding 8). The amounts here are before GST; GST (Commonwealth law, not deposited) is added on top.
-- Sch 2 cl 2(1): "(a) for all work involved in a limited claim where the identity of the offender is known and
-- compensation is agreed -- $700 (indexed); (b) for all work involved in a claim that is not a limited claim or a related
-- claim -- $1 400 (indexed); (c) for all work involved in a claim that is a related claim -- (i) for the first claim --
-- $1 400 (indexed); and (ii) for each of the other related claims -- $1 100 (indexed)." (2): "an application to the court
-- for approval of settlement of a claim made by a person under a disability is $350 (indexed)". cl 3: counsel, "(a) for
-- all work preparatory to an application to the court for compensation ... and for the first 5 hours of the hearing ...
-- $1 000 (indexed); (b) for each hour or part of an hour after the first 5 hours of the hearing -- $200 (indexed); (c)
-- for an opinion as to the settlement of a claim for compensation made by a person under a disability -- $700 (indexed);
-- (d) for an opinion as to the settlement of a related claim ... made by a person under a disability -- $500 (indexed)."
-- cl 3A: "The prescribed amount in relation to costs for an appeal is $700 (indexed)."
DECLARE `Kind of claim for legal costs` IS ONE OF
    `a limited claim (grief, funeral expenses or both)`
    `the first of related claims`
    `one of the other related claims`
    `any other claim`

DECLARE `Legal costs facts` HAS
    `kind of claim`                                                         IS A `Kind of claim for legal costs`
    `the identity of the offender is known`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `compensation is agreed`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `an application to the court for compensation is made`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours of the hearing of the application`                               IS A NUMBER
    `the claim is by a person under a disability and the court must approve the settlement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is an appeal`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Legal costs answer` IS ONE OF
    `the prescribed amount, before GST, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: Schedule 2 clause 2(1) prescribes no amount for a limited claim unless the offender is known and compensation is agreed`

GIVEN c IS A `Legal costs facts`, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the solicitor's prescribed amount (Sch 2 cl 2(1))` c p MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `kind of claim`
    WHEN `a limited claim (grief, funeral expenses or both)` THEN
        IF c's `the identity of the offender is known` AND c's `compensation is agreed`
        THEN JUST (`the indexed amount of` 700 `at` p)
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `the first of related claims`      THEN JUST (`the indexed amount of` 1400 `at` p)
    WHEN `one of the other related claims`  THEN JUST (`the indexed amount of` 1100 `at` p)
    WHEN `any other claim`                  THEN JUST (`the indexed amount of` 1400 `at` p)

GIVEN c IS A `Legal costs facts`, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the counsel's prescribed amount for the court application (Sch 2 cl 3(a), (b))` c p MEANS
    IF NOT (c's `an application to the court for compensation is made`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the indexed amount of` 1000 `at` p
         PLUS (`whole or part units in` (`the larger number of` 0 `and` (c's `hours of the hearing of the application` MINUS 5)) TIMES `the indexed amount of` 200 `at` p)

GIVEN c IS A `Legal costs facts`, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the prescribed amounts for a settlement for a person under a disability (Sch 2 cl 2(2), cl 3(c), (d))` c p MEANS
    IF NOT (c's `the claim is by a person under a disability and the court must approve the settlement`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the indexed amount of` 350 `at` p PLUS `the counsel's opinion`
    WHERE
        `the counsel's opinion` MEANS
            IF    c's `kind of claim` EQUALS `the first of related claims`
               OR c's `kind of claim` EQUALS `one of the other related claims`
            THEN `the indexed amount of` 500 `at` p
            ELSE `the indexed amount of` 700 `at` p

-- The total prescribed for the claim: what costs awarded may not exceed and what a legal practitioner may charge or seek
-- to recover (s 25(1)(a), (b)), before GST. Disbursements (cl 4) are separate and are not encoded.
GIVEN `the day the proceedings commence` IS A DATE, cpi IS A `CPI figures for s 4(2)`, c IS A `Legal costs facts`
GIVETH A `Legal costs answer`
`s 25(1) -- the most that may be charged or awarded for costs` `the day the proceedings commence` cpi c MEANS
    CONSIDER `the solicitor's prescribed amount (Sch 2 cl 2(1))` c p
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered: Schedule 2 clause 2(1) prescribes no amount for a limited claim unless the offender is known and compensation is agreed`
    WHEN JUST s THEN
        `the prescribed amount, before GST, is`
            (s PLUS `the counsel's prescribed amount for the court application (Sch 2 cl 3(a), (b))` c p
               PLUS `the prescribed amounts for a settlement for a person under a disability (Sch 2 cl 2(2), cl 3(c), (d))` c p
               PLUS (IF c's `there is an appeal` THEN `the indexed amount of` 700 `at` p ELSE 0))
    WHERE
        p MEANS `the s 4(2) proportion in force on` `the day the proceedings commence` `with` cpi

§§ `Regulative rules -- the claimant`

-- Clock: days, counted from the day each rule starts. The Crown Solicitor, the Crown and the court are officials and get
-- no seat; what they may do appears as what the claimant must do and when. READING: applying is the claimant's choice.
-- The time limits are written as MUST ... LEST BREACH so that a trace that ends in that BREACH says the claim is out of
-- time (unless the court extends the period, s 18(7)), not that the claimant did wrong.
DECLARE `VOCA party` IS ONE OF `the claimant`, `the Crown`

DECLARE `VOCA act` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the Crown Solicitor, with the information and documents required, verified by statutory declaration`
    `apply to the Crown Solicitor without the required information, documents or statutory declaration`
    `apply to the court for an order for statutory compensation`
    `serve a copy of the court application on the offender`
    `require the claimant to submit to a medical examination`
    `submit to a medical examination by a medical practitioner nominated by the Crown`

-- s 18(1): the person "may, within the initial application period, apply"; (3): "to the Crown Solicitor" in the first
-- instance; (4): the application "must (i) contain the information required by the regulations; and (ii) be accompanied
-- by any medical reports relevant to the injury ...; and (iii) be accompanied by any further documents required under the
-- regulations; and (b) the information contained in an application must be verified by statutory declaration."
-- Clock starts on the day of the offence (or of the death); the seat works out the days to the last day. READING: an
-- application without the s 18(4) contents is not an application "made" under s 18, so it does not stop the clock.
GIVEN `days to the last day of the initial application period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOCA party` `VOCA act`
DECIDE `s 18(1)-(4) -- the claimant must apply to the Crown Solicitor, with the prescribed contents verified by statutory declaration, within the initial application period` IS
    PARTY  `the claimant`
    MUST   `apply to the Crown Solicitor, with the information and documents required, verified by statutory declaration`
    WITHIN `days to the last day of the initial application period`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 18(1)-(4): no complete, verified application to the Crown Solicitor within the initial application period (3 years after the offence, or 12 months after the death); the claim is out of time unless the court extends the period (s 18(7))"

-- s 19(2): "A claimant who makes an application to the court must (subject to this section) serve a copy of the
-- application on the offender." (3)(a): "if the identity of the offender is not known, there is no need to serve"; (b)
-- "the court may, on application by a claimant, exempt the claimant". No time is stated.
GIVEN `the identity of the offender is known` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has exempted the claimant from serving the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant must serve the offender (s 19(2), (3))` `the identity of the offender is known` `the court has exempted the claimant from serving the offender` IF
    `the identity of the offender is known` AND (NOT `the court has exempted the claimant from serving the offender`)

GIVEN `the identity of the offender is known` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has exempted the claimant from serving the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOCA party` `VOCA act`
DECIDE `s 19(2), (3) -- a claimant who applies to the court must serve a copy on the offender, unless the offender is unknown or the court exempts the claimant` IS
    IF `the claimant must serve the offender (s 19(2), (3))` `the identity of the offender is known` `the court has exempted the claimant from serving the offender`
    THEN PARTY `the claimant`
         MUST  `serve a copy of the court application on the offender`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 19(2): a claimant who applies to the court must serve a copy of the application on the offender"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 18(5), (6): if the claim is not settled in the period for negotiation, "the claimant may apply to the court", and the
-- application "must be made on or before the later of" the end of the initial application period and 6 months after the
-- period for negotiation. Clock starts on the last day of the period for negotiation; the seat works out the days to the
-- s 18(6) day. Once the claimant applies, s 19(2) follows.
GIVEN `the claim was settled by agreement within the period for negotiation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days from the end of the period for negotiation to the last day to apply to the court` IS A NUMBER
      `the identity of the offender is known` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has exempted the claimant from serving the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOCA party` `VOCA act`
DECIDE `s 18(5), (6), s 19(2) -- if the claim is not settled, the claimant must apply to the court by the s 18(6) day, and then serve the offender` IS
    IF `the claim was settled by agreement within the period for negotiation`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY  `the claimant`
         MUST   `apply to the court for an order for statutory compensation`
         WITHIN `days from the end of the period for negotiation to the last day to apply to the court`
         HENCE  `s 19(2), (3) -- a claimant who applies to the court must serve a copy on the offender, unless the offender is unknown or the court exempts the claimant` `the identity of the offender is known` `the court has exempted the claimant from serving the offender`
         LEST   BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 18(6): no application to the court by the later of the end of the initial application period and 6 months after the period for negotiation; the claim is out of time unless the court extends the period (s 18(7))"

-- s 21(1): "A claimant must, if the Crown so requires, submit himself or herself for medical examination by a medical
-- practitioner nominated by the Crown." (2): its costs, and the claimant's reasonable expenses of complying, "must be
-- borne by the Crown". No time is stated.
GIVEN `the Crown has required a medical examination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOCA party` `VOCA act`
DECIDE `s 21(1) -- a claimant must submit to a medical examination if the Crown requires it, at the Crown's cost` IS
    IF `the Crown has required a medical examination`
    THEN PARTY `the claimant`
         MUST  `submit to a medical examination by a medical practitioner nominated by the Crown`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 21(1): a claimant must submit to a medical examination by a medical practitioner nominated by the Crown when the Crown requires it"
    ELSE FULFILLED
